  "reasoning": "The facts describe three distinct criminal conduct by the public official. First, he used his position to obtain cash, shopping cards and gold from companies and individuals in exchange for favorable treatment, which constitutes the crime of accepting bribes (受贿). Second, he unilaterally transferred public funds of the state‑owned housing construction company to a private individual without proper approval, which is the crime of embezzling public funds (挪用公款). Third, his personal assets far exceed his lawful income and a large portion cannot be explained, indicating the crime of receiving a huge amount of property that cannot be accounted for (收受巨额财物). Therefore the appropriate charges are: 受贿;挪用公款;收受巨额财物.",
  "final_answer": "[罪名]受贿;挪用公款;收受巨额财物<eoa>"
